      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Favourable balance (Debit Balance), as per the Cash Book, is an asset to an account holder. It is also known as debit balance as per the Cash Book. Favourable balance is the excess of total of debit side over total of credit side of a bank column of a Cash Book.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, a favourable balance indicates a positive cash position for the account holder.",
